<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">Document Approval and Workflow Routing</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">
            Structured document approval ensuring proper authorization through configurable workflows 
            with digital signatures, deadline enforcement, and comprehensive audit documentation.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Configurable Workflow Design</h2>
        <p>
            Workflow templates define approval paths for document types matching organizational 
            authorization requirements. Contract reviews route through legal and management while 
            expense reports follow financial approval hierarchies. Each workflow stage specifies 
            required approvers, deadlines, and escalation rules.
        </p>
        <p>
            Sequential workflows move documents through approval stages in order with each 
            approver reviewing the document after previous approvals. Parallel workflows enable 
            simultaneous review by multiple stakeholders when independent approvals accelerate 
            processing without compromising control.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Digital Signature Integration</h2>
        <p>
            Digital signature capture applies legally binding signatures to documents using 
            certificate-based authentication and signature pad interfaces. Signatures embed 
            into PDF documents creating tamper-evident records with signer identity, timestamp, 
            and document hash verification.
        </p>
        <p>
            The signature pipeline uses PdfSharp and BouncyCastle for certificate handling with 
            QuestPDF for document generation creating professional signed outputs suitable for 
            regulatory submission and legal presentation.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Deadline and Escalation Management</h2>
        <p>
            Workflow deadlines establish service level expectations with automatic reminders 
            as deadlines approach. Escalation rules route overdue documents to supervisors 
            or alternative approvers ensuring business processes continue without manual 
            intervention when primary approvers are unavailable.
        </p>
        <p>
            Audit trails capture every workflow action including initiations, approvals, 
            rejections, reassignments, and comments with timestamps and IP addresses. This 
            comprehensive logging supports compliance requirements and dispute resolution.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

